b8=$.c==="en"
b9=b8?"XXcross: cross plus two pairs":"XXcross: d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng k\xe8m 2 c\u1eb7p"
c0=b8?"The next step after X-cross: build two F2L pairs during the cross.":"B\u01b0\u1edbc ti\u1ebfp theo c\u1ee7a X-cross: g\u1ed9p 2 c\u1eb7p F2L v\xe0o l\xfac l\xe0m d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng."
c1=b8?"Only try once X-cross feels easy: planning two pairs in 15 seconds is hard \u2013 don't overrun inspection.":"Ch\u1ec9 th\u1eed khi X-cross \u0111\xe3 quen: l\xean k\u1ebf ho\u1ea1ch 2 c\u1eb7p trong 15 gi\xe2y l\xe0 r\u1ea5t kh\xf3, \u0111\u1eebng \u0111\u1ec3 qu\xe1 gi\u1edd quan s\xe1t."
r=b8?"Easiest when the two pairs belong to ADJACENT slots and the cross edge between them is already in place: you are really building a 2\xd72\xd73 block.":"D\u1ec5 l\xe0m nh\u1ea5t khi 2 c\u1eb7p thu\u1ed9c 2 khe K\u1ec0 nhau v\xe0 c\u1ea1nh d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng gi\u1eefa ch\xfang \u0111\xe3 n\u1eb1m s\u1eb5n: th\u1ef1c ch\u1ea5t l\xe0 d\u1ef1ng m\u1ed9t kh\u1ed1i 2\xd72\xd73."
q=b8?"Can't see it all? Plan the X-cross and look for the second pair while turning \u2013 still faster than stopping.":"Kh\xf4ng th\u1ea5y \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c h\u1ebft? L\xean k\u1ebf ho\u1ea1ch X-cross, r\u1ed3i trong l\xfac l\xe0m th\xec t\xecm c\u1eb7p th\u1ee9 hai \u2013 v\u1eabn nhanh h\u01a1n d\u1eebng l\u1ea1i."
c1=A.a([c1,r,q,b8?"Practise: solve crosses in the Cross trainer, then count how many pairs you could have added.":"Luy\u1ec7n: gi\u1ea3i d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng \u1edf m\xe0n Luy\u1ec7n d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng, sau \u0111\xf3 t\u1ef1 \u0111\u1ebfm xem c\xf3 th\u1ec3 g\u1ed9p \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c m\u1ea5y c\u1eb7p."],s)
b8=$.c==="en"
r=b8?"FreeFOP: blocks instead of a cross":"FreeFOP: d\u1ef1ng kh\u1ed1i thay cho d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng"
q=b8?"Know what FreeFOP is and when to try it.":"Bi\u1ebft FreeFOP l\xe0 g\xec v\xe0 khi n\xe0o n\xean th\u1eed."
p=b8?'FreeFOP = "Free" + F2L + OLL + PLL: instead of a cross then pairs, freely build a 2\xd72\xd72 or 2\xd72\xd73 block, then finish the rest of F2L.':'FreeFOP = "Free" + F2L + OLL + PLL: thay v\xec l\xe0m d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng r\u1ed3i t\u1eebng c\u1eb7p, d\u1ef1ng t\u1ef1 do m\u1ed9t kh\u1ed1i 2\xd72\xd72 ho\u1eb7c 2\xd72\xd73, sau \u0111\xf3 ho\xe0n th\xe0nh ph\u1ea7n F2L c\xf2n l\u1ea1i.'
o=b8?"Pros: fewer moves when the cube has a block ready; the last layer is still the OLL/PLL you know.":"\u01afu \u0111i\u1ec3m: \xedt b\u01b0\u1edbc h\u01a1n khi cube c\xf3 s\u1eb5n kh\u1ed1i; t\u1ea7ng cu\u1ed1i v\u1eabn l\xe0 OLL/PLL quen thu\u1ed9c n\xean kh\xf4ng ph\u1ea3i h\u1ecdc l\u1ea1i."
n=b8?'Cons: harder look-ahead than CFOP, needs strong inspection. Most fast solvers stay with CFOP and "borrow" the block idea on easy scrambles.':'Nh\u01b0\u1ee3c \u0111i\u1ec3m: kh\xf3 nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc h\u01a1n CFOP, c\u1ea7n quan s\xe1t gi\u1ecfi. Ph\u1ea7n l\u1edbn ng\u01b0\u1eddi gi\u1ea3i nhanh v\u1eabn d\xf9ng CFOP v\xe0 ch\u1ec9 "m\u01b0\u1ee3n" \xfd t\u01b0\u1edfng kh\u1ed1i khi g\u1eb7p x\xe1o d\u1ec5.'
m=b8?"A 2\xd72\xd72 block: one white corner + its 3 edges + 3 centres. Look around for a corner that already has 1\u20132 edges attached.":"Kh\u1ed1i 2\xd72\xd72: m\u1ed9t g\xf3c tr\u1eafng + 3 c\u1ea1nh quanh n\xf3 + 3 t\xe2m. Nh\xecn quanh cube xem g\xf3c n\xe0o \u0111\xe3 c\xf3 s\u1eb5n 1\u20132 c\u1ea1nh d\xednh v\xe0o."
p=A.a([p,o,n,m,b8?"Want to really build blocks? Try Roux (Learn \u2192 Roux & ZZ) \u2013 the whole method is block-building.":"Mu\u1ed1n d\u1ef1ng kh\u1ed1i th\u1eadt s\u1ef1? Xem Roux (H\u1ecdc \u2192 Roux & ZZ) \u2013 c\u1ea3 ph\u01b0\u01a1ng ph\xe1p l\xe0 d\u1ef1ng kh\u1ed1i."],s)
b8=$.c==="en"
o=b8?"Efficient F2L: pick pairs, no rotations":"F2L hi\u1ec7u qu\u1ea3: ch\u1ecdn c\u1eb7p, kh\xf4ng xoay cube"
n=b8?"Cut moves and pauses in F2L \u2013 half of your solve time.":"Gi\u1ea3m s\u1ed1 b\u01b0\u1edbc v\xe0 s\u1ed1 l\u1ea7n d\u1eebng \u1edf F2L \u2013 ph\u1ea7n chi\u1ebfm n\u1eeda th\u1eddi gian gi\u1ea3i."
m=b8?"No fixed order: each time pick the EASIEST pair (visible in the top layer, fewest moves).":"Kh\xf4ng l\xe0m theo th\u1ee9 t\u1ef1 c\u1ed1 \u0111\u1ecbnh: m\u1ed7i l\u1ea7n ch\u1ecdn c\u1eb7p D\u1ec4 nh\u1ea5t (\u0111\xe3 l\u1ed9 ra \u1edf t\u1ea7ng tr\xean, \xedt b\u01b0\u1edbc nh\u1ea5t)."
l=b8?"Insert into back slots with R' U' R or L U L' instead of rotating y2 (see lesson F2L 4).":"Ch\xe8n v\xe0o khe sau b\u1eb1ng R' U' R ho\u1eb7c L U L' thay v\xec xoay y2 (xem b\xe0i F2L 4)."
k=b8?"Pair at the back of the top layer: turn U to bring it forward \u2013 a U turn beats a cube rotation.":"C\u1eb7p \u1edf m\u1eb7t sau t\u1ea7ng tr\xean: xoay U \u0111\u01b0a ra tr\u01b0\u1edbc r\u1ed3i m\u1edbi x\u1eed l\xfd \u2013 U nhanh h\u01a1n xoay c\u1ea3 cube."
j=b8?"Use an empty slot to set up a pair: an unsolved slot can be used to split/join instead of a long sequence.":"D\xf9ng khe tr\u1ed1ng \u0111\u1ec3 gh\xe9p c\u1eb7p: n\u1ebfu m\u1ed9t khe ch\u01b0a l\xe0m, c\xf3 th\u1ec3 d\xf9ng n\xf3 \u0111\u1ec3 t\xe1ch/gh\xe9p thay cho b\u01b0\u1edbc r\u01b0\u1eddm r\xe0."
m=A.a([m,l,k,j,b8?"While inserting a pair, your eyes should already be finding the next one (see Trick 10: Look-ahead).":"Ch\xe8n xong c\u1eb7p n\xe0y, m\u1eaft \u0111\xe3 ph\u1ea3i t\xecm c\u1eb7p ti\u1ebfp theo (xem Trick 10: Nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc)."],s)
