g2=f9?'"Headlights" = 2 corners of the same colour on one side.':'"\u0110\xe8n pha" = 2 g\xf3c c\xf9ng m\xe0u tr\xean m\u1ed9t m\u1eb7t b\xean.'
g3=f9?"Headlights on 1 side: turn U so the headlights are on the LEFT, do T-perm.":"C\xf3 \u0111\xe8n pha \u1edf 1 m\u1eb7t: xoay U \u0111\u1ec3 \u0111\xe8n pha \u1edf b\xean TR\xc1I, l\xe0m T-perm."
g4=f9?"No headlights: do Y-perm.":"Kh\xf4ng c\xf3 \u0111\xe8n pha: l\xe0m Y-perm."
g5=f9?"Headlights on all 4 sides: corners are done, move on to the edges.":"C\u1ea3 4 m\u1eb7t c\xf3 \u0111\xe8n pha: g\xf3c \u0111\xe3 xong, sang b\u01b0\u1edbc c\u1ea1nh."
g2=A.a([g2,g3,g4,g5,f9?"Want fewer algorithms? The Trick 6 shortcut uses A-perm (headlights at the BACK) for both cases.":"Mu\u1ed1n \xedt c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c h\u01a1n? \u0110\u01b0\u1eddng t\u1eaft \u1edf Trick 6 d\xf9ng A-perm (\u0111\xe8n pha \u1edf SAU) cho c\u1ea3 2 tr\u01b0\u1eddng h\u1ee3p."],s)
